      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2004 Excerpta Medica, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "There are limited data regarding the effect of race on survival after percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) in the modern era. The investigators analyzed the impact of race on 3-year survival in 3,783 consecutive patients who underwent PCI in 1998 and 1999."
